1
00:00:01,109 --> 00:00:02,308
(New Me)

2
00:00:02,309 --> 00:00:04,149
(New Me?)

3
00:00:04,309 --> 00:00:06,879
- Nice to see you all. - Nice to see you.

4
00:00:07,079 --> 00:00:09,218
We have an important announcement today.

5
00:00:09,219 --> 00:00:10,948
- What? - My gosh.

6
00:00:10,949 --> 00:00:12,018
- What is it? - What?

7
00:00:12,019 --> 00:00:13,118
- What is that? - All right.

8
00:00:13,119 --> 00:00:14,319
- What? - Pass them down.

9
00:00:14,489 --> 00:00:15,788
- "Newsletter?" - What's this?

10
00:00:15,789 --> 00:00:17,828
- What is this? - It's like passing down test paper.

11
00:00:17,829 --> 00:00:19,359
- It's the newsletter. - My gosh.

12
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:20,798
I haven't gotten one of these in a long time.

13
00:00:20,799 --> 00:00:22,398
To make it look old-school, I printed it on pulp paper.

14
00:00:22,399 --> 00:00:24,369
- Pulp paper! - This brings back old memories.

15
00:00:25,129 --> 00:00:26,199
So...

16
00:00:26,339 --> 00:00:27,768
- Let's take a look. - Okay.

17
00:00:27,769 --> 00:00:29,008
This looks like a real newsletter.

18
00:00:29,009 --> 00:00:31,639
We'll go on a summer retreat soon.

19
00:00:32,179 --> 00:00:34,279
We'll stay at a youth hostel just like the old days.

20
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:35,948
- A youth hostel? - We're going to a youth hostel.

21
00:00:35,949 --> 00:00:37,078
It's been so long.

22
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:38,449
- At last. - I'm excited.

23
00:00:38,979 --> 00:00:40,248
"Verdurous early summer."

24
00:00:40,249 --> 00:00:42,249
We haven't seen a phrase like this in a long time.

25
00:00:43,289 --> 00:00:44,488
It's a community program.

26
00:00:44,489 --> 00:00:46,389
Will you play "By Love" by Sunflower?

27
00:00:47,959 --> 00:00:48,988
(Precious memories with the members)

28
00:00:48,989 --> 00:00:50,328
- I love it. - It's one of the regular meetings?

29
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:51,359
A retreat?

30
00:00:52,429 --> 00:00:54,358
We'll become one at the retreat. Right?

31
00:00:54,359 --> 00:00:55,599
We'll go on a summer retreat.

32
00:00:56,299 --> 00:00:57,728
What if there's a drill sergeant?

33
00:00:57,729 --> 00:00:58,739
A drill sergeant?

34
00:00:59,169 --> 00:01:00,368
Things we need to bring...

35
00:01:00,369 --> 00:01:02,608
We have to bring a random ingredient for bibimbap.

36
00:01:02,609 --> 00:01:04,139
- This is important. - What's this?

37
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:06,208
We'll have random bibimbap for lunch.

38
00:01:06,209 --> 00:01:08,709
It's quite trendy among the zoomers.

39
00:01:08,809 --> 00:01:10,708
- What? - We'll each bring an ingredient...

40
00:01:10,709 --> 00:01:11,709
and mix bibimbap.

41
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:13,079
We can just bring any ingredient?

42
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:16,218
Just bring one ingredient without discussing.

43
00:01:16,219 --> 00:01:17,448
(I see.)

44
00:01:17,449 --> 00:01:18,619
- Sir. - Yes?

45
00:01:18,689 --> 00:01:19,959
Will Dae Ho...

46
00:01:20,489 --> 00:01:22,689
and Kian84 bring food too?

47
00:01:23,429 --> 00:01:24,689
What do you mean?

48
00:01:25,799 --> 00:01:27,759
(Last fall at the Innocent Moo-Ku Fall Field Day)

49
00:01:28,799 --> 00:01:31,569
(His kimchi fried rice made him speechless.)

50
00:01:31,829 --> 00:01:32,838
It's bibimbap.

51
00:01:32,839 --> 00:01:36,709
(Dae Ho's bibimbap from the dead)

52
00:01:36,809 --> 00:01:37,909
- My gosh. - Goodness.

53
00:01:38,109 --> 00:01:39,485
Unfortunately, that will be the case.

54
00:01:39,509 --> 00:01:41,539
- I have a question too. - Go ahead.

55
00:01:41,639 --> 00:01:44,548
Is it possible to leave out ingredients if we don't want to?

56
00:01:44,549 --> 00:01:45,649
We must add everything.

57
00:01:46,279 --> 00:01:47,418
- Because... - That's...

58
00:01:47,419 --> 00:01:49,289
- We're one. - We are?

59
00:01:49,549 --> 00:01:50,848
Let's not invite Dae Ho.

60
00:01:50,849 --> 00:01:52,888
(Then let's not invite Dae Ho.)

61
00:01:52,889 --> 00:01:53,889
Not Dae Ho.

62
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:55,290
- Hey. - Even I can't eat his food.

63
00:01:55,659 --> 00:01:57,529
He eats weird food.

64
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,828
It just looked unappetizing. But the food wasn't spoiled.

65
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,569
- Okay. - Wait.

66
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,428
- There will be a talent show. - Yes.

67
00:02:04,429 --> 00:02:06,368
Will there be a prize if you win first place...

68
00:02:06,369 --> 00:02:07,538
or something?

69
00:02:07,539 --> 00:02:09,268
- Actually, - There's a prize?

70
00:02:09,269 --> 00:02:11,409
I prepared the best prizes this time.

71
00:02:11,869 --> 00:02:13,339
You guys might fight over them.

72
00:02:13,809 --> 00:02:15,925
The prizes will be better than the ones at the fall field day.

73
00:02:15,949 --> 00:02:17,108
- Really? - They will be better?

74
00:02:17,109 --> 00:02:19,018
There will be amazing prizes. I daresay they're the best ones yet.

75
00:02:19,019 --> 00:02:21,879
We're meeting up at the MBC building in Sangam at 10am.

76
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:23,765
We'll leave on time even if you're late.

77
00:02:23,789 --> 00:02:24,848
I have to host a radio show.

78
00:02:24,849 --> 00:02:26,119
Remember the school retreat?

79
00:02:26,219 --> 00:02:27,518
I really love this project.

80
00:02:27,519 --> 00:02:29,258
It's been 30 years since I had been on a retreat.

81
00:02:29,259 --> 00:02:30,288
- Really? - Yes.

82
00:02:30,289 --> 00:02:31,888
- Think about my age. - I haven't used the word,

83
00:02:31,889 --> 00:02:33,398
- "retreat." - Right.

84
00:02:33,399 --> 00:02:35,228
- I'm already excited. I won't... - Me too.

85
00:02:35,229 --> 00:02:36,699
I won't be able to sleep now.

86
00:02:36,999 --> 00:02:38,028
I'll be too excited. I'm serious.

87
00:02:38,029 --> 00:02:39,098
- No more questions, right? - No.

88
00:02:39,099 --> 00:02:41,199
Don't forget that we have some amazing prizes.

89
00:02:41,469 --> 00:02:43,108
- Great. - Thirteen people.

90
00:02:43,109 --> 00:02:44,149
I'm looking forward to it.

91
00:02:44,669 --> 00:02:46,978
(A Lucky Day)

92
00:02:46,979 --> 00:02:49,809
(Snoring)

93
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:55,079
(It's pitch-dark in the room.)

94
00:02:56,049 --> 00:02:58,048
(Snorting)

95
00:02:58,049 --> 00:03:00,059
That's the kind of sound I make.

96
00:03:01,019 --> 00:03:02,329
(Is that me?)

97
00:03:03,359 --> 00:03:04,529
I snored like that?

98
00:03:04,929 --> 00:03:07,629
Shin Young, you should buy the CPAP machine.

99
00:03:08,029 --> 00:03:09,429
- What's wrong with me? - That's...

100
00:03:10,099 --> 00:03:11,169
- My goodness. - Wait.

101
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:13,499
- You didn't know you snored? - No.

102
00:03:13,799 --> 00:03:15,609
I thought I didn't snore.

103
00:03:16,939 --> 00:03:20,479
(Getting up)

104
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:26,949
(She gets up right away.)

105
00:03:28,149 --> 00:03:29,149
(Spraying)

106
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:31,919
(Spraying)

107
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:33,918
(Getting rid of mites as soon as she gets up)

108
00:03:33,919 --> 00:03:35,258
You do that to get rid of mites.

109
00:03:35,259 --> 00:03:37,129
That's my daily routine.

110
00:03:37,289 --> 00:03:38,289
That's nice.

111
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:40,949
- I like that you're clean. - We should have a clean lifestyle.

112
00:03:48,809 --> 00:03:50,869
(Frowning)

113
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:57,879
(She wakes up late past noon.)

114
00:03:58,549 --> 00:04:00,579
Today is my day off.

115
00:04:01,519 --> 00:04:04,719
So I'm having a day off today.

116
00:04:05,789 --> 00:04:07,819
It's been three weeks since I had a day off.

117
00:04:08,659 --> 00:04:11,989
I had a pile of household chores waiting for me.

118
00:04:12,359 --> 00:04:15,528
I only thought about doing them because I was so busy with work.

119
00:04:15,529 --> 00:04:17,609
When I came home, I took a shower and went to sleep.

120
00:04:17,869 --> 00:04:20,739
There's a list of chores I never got a chance to take care of.

121
00:04:21,439 --> 00:04:22,938
I'm going to do all of them today.

122
00:04:22,939 --> 00:04:25,209
(She'll take care of the chores on her day off.)

123
00:04:26,179 --> 00:04:28,379
(Grabbing)

124
00:04:29,949 --> 00:04:34,279
(Let me turn on the AC first.)

125
00:04:39,989 --> 00:04:41,749
Gosh, the temperature at your house is 30°C?

126
00:04:41,789 --> 00:04:44,059
- The temperature is at 29°C? - It's hot in the house.

127
00:04:46,229 --> 00:04:48,699
(Warm)

128
00:04:49,799 --> 00:04:52,099
(Darn it...)

129
00:04:54,099 --> 00:04:55,398
(The house is getting warmer, not cool.)

130
00:04:55,399 --> 00:04:58,169
It must be really hot in the house if it's at 29°C.

131
00:04:59,379 --> 00:05:01,608
(Let me just turn it off.)

132
00:05:01,609 --> 00:05:02,609
(Sighing)

133
00:05:05,649 --> 00:05:06,679
The air conditioner is...

134
00:05:07,619 --> 00:05:08,649
broken.

135
00:05:09,489 --> 00:05:11,388
- It's the cooling gas. - When the weather is so hot?

136
00:05:11,389 --> 00:05:12,588
- The cooling gas? - It ran out of the cooling gas.

137
00:05:12,589 --> 00:05:13,688
I couldn't recharge the refrigerant.

138
00:05:13,689 --> 00:05:15,388
You need to call someone for that.

139
00:05:15,389 --> 00:05:17,328
- Right. They'll come in September. - You need to.

140
00:05:17,329 --> 00:05:18,388
What? Really?

141
00:05:18,389 --> 00:05:20,098
The backlog is crazy.

142
00:05:20,099 --> 00:05:22,368
I bet everyone is calling the engineers now.

143
00:05:22,369 --> 00:05:24,369
I tried to last one summer without the AC.

144
00:05:24,529 --> 00:05:25,968
But I ended up sleeping in a motel.

145
00:05:25,969 --> 00:05:27,438
- I bet it was super cool. - Right.

146
00:05:27,439 --> 00:05:29,069
- I couldn't stay at home. - Right.

147
00:05:29,209 --> 00:05:30,969
So I'm looking into more options.

148
00:05:32,779 --> 00:05:35,479
(Should I open up the window?)

149
00:05:37,009 --> 00:05:38,578
What if it's cooler outside?

150
00:05:38,579 --> 00:05:39,619
My gosh.

151
00:05:41,249 --> 00:05:45,389
(She opens the window and feels the air outside.)

152
00:05:46,159 --> 00:05:47,788
- Gosh, it's hot. - It was super hot that day.

153
00:05:47,789 --> 00:05:49,158
It's really hot in the afternoon.

154
00:05:49,159 --> 00:05:51,628
- I can see it in your face. - My gosh. It was so hot.

155
00:05:51,629 --> 00:05:53,058
- I can feel the heat too. - It drove me crazy.

156
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:54,129
- Yes. - It's hot.

157
00:05:54,859 --> 00:05:56,468
It's hot.

158
00:05:56,469 --> 00:05:59,569
(She runs away to the bathroom for now.)

159
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:07,109
(Washing her face)

160
00:06:08,079 --> 00:06:10,779
(Scrubbing)

161
00:06:12,149 --> 00:06:13,348
It cools you down only for a minute.

162
00:06:13,349 --> 00:06:14,378
(She quickly washes down the heat.)

163
00:06:14,379 --> 00:06:16,019
She should splash some water on her back.

164
00:06:16,549 --> 00:06:17,718
What?

165
00:06:17,719 --> 00:06:19,119
- Are you washing your hair? - Yes.

166
00:06:19,459 --> 00:06:20,758
I bought that faucet,

167
00:06:20,759 --> 00:06:22,459
so I could wash my hair over the basin.

168
00:06:23,289 --> 00:06:26,629
- So you can freely move it around? - Yes. That's right.

169
00:06:29,199 --> 00:06:31,068
Look at the back of her head. It's smooth.

170
00:06:31,069 --> 00:06:32,599
- I shaved it. - I see.

171
00:06:33,499 --> 00:06:34,868
(She shaves the back of her head herself.)

172
00:06:34,869 --> 00:06:36,069
You wear a Two Block haircut.

173
00:06:37,769 --> 00:06:40,439
(It's still smooth as she shaves it herself.)

174
00:06:41,239 --> 00:06:42,949
(Scrubbing hard)

175
00:06:43,449 --> 00:06:45,779
(Thoroughly cleaning it with shampoo)

176
00:06:46,749 --> 00:06:49,949
(Rinsing her smooth nape completely)

177
00:06:51,149 --> 00:06:52,589
That's not Sung Hwan.

178
00:06:54,619 --> 00:06:56,358
Just in case you didn't know.

179
00:06:56,359 --> 00:06:57,428
When I was watching it, I was like...

180
00:06:57,429 --> 00:06:59,758
- That's not Sung Hwan. - "Wait. When did I film that?"

181
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:00,928
That's not Sung Hwan.

182
00:07:00,929 --> 00:07:02,058
It's Shin Young.

183
00:07:02,059 --> 00:07:03,368
(It's Shin Young with a shaved nape.)

184
00:07:03,369 --> 00:07:04,469
What's this?

185
00:07:06,269 --> 00:07:07,338
All right.

186
00:07:07,339 --> 00:07:10,139
(Oh, that's nice and cool.)

187
00:07:12,009 --> 00:07:13,139
(She brushes her teeth too.)

188
00:07:13,239 --> 00:07:15,609
(Retching)

189
00:07:15,809 --> 00:07:17,178
- That's not me. - It's not Sung Hwan.

190
00:07:17,179 --> 00:07:18,648
- It's not me. - That's not Sung Hwan.

191
00:07:18,649 --> 00:07:19,649
(It's me.)

192
00:07:20,019 --> 00:07:21,279
My gosh. Let's see.

193
00:07:21,679 --> 00:07:24,319
(After cooling down in the bathroom, she goes to the kitchen.)

194
00:07:24,689 --> 00:07:26,959
(I need to eat even on a hot day.)

195
00:07:27,459 --> 00:07:29,489
(Opening up)

196
00:07:32,659 --> 00:07:34,698
(She grabs an ingredient without hesitation.)

197
00:07:34,699 --> 00:07:36,098
What's she going to eat for her first meal?

198
00:07:36,099 --> 00:07:37,899
(She grabs an ingredient without hesitation.)

199
00:07:39,339 --> 00:07:40,499
- Pork belly. - Pork belly.

200
00:07:41,099 --> 00:07:42,239
I just woke up, so...

201
00:07:43,869 --> 00:07:46,209
(I love it.)

202
00:07:46,779 --> 00:07:49,348
I always eat pork belly in the morning.

203
00:07:49,349 --> 00:07:51,549
It's either pork belly or bulgogi.

204
00:07:51,779 --> 00:07:54,349
Or I eat braised kimchi with ribs.

205
00:07:54,549 --> 00:07:57,348
I often eat meat for my first meal of the day.

206
00:07:57,349 --> 00:07:59,019
(Shin Young's breakfast is full of meat.)

207
00:07:59,559 --> 00:08:00,588
I need energy.

208
00:08:00,589 --> 00:08:03,489
Our breakfast should be as grand as a royal meal.

209
00:08:03,589 --> 00:08:05,859
We must eat like a king for breakfast to be healthy.

210
00:08:06,159 --> 00:08:08,499
Our lunch should be simple like the commoners' meal.

211
00:08:08,929 --> 00:08:11,229
Then our dinner should be scarce...

212
00:08:11,399 --> 00:08:14,369
like the servants' meal from the old days.

213
00:08:14,639 --> 00:08:17,119
But your breakfast and dinner are both grand like royal meals.

214
00:08:17,369 --> 00:08:19,109
You eat like a king for all three meals.

215
00:08:19,909 --> 00:08:21,578
My dinner is scarce like the servants' meal.

216
00:08:21,579 --> 00:08:23,459
You know that servants eat everything they see.

217
00:08:23,549 --> 00:08:24,679
Right.

218
00:08:25,049 --> 00:08:27,249
(Food is the best.)

219
00:08:28,179 --> 00:08:31,349
(An original diet following the hierarchy system)

220
00:08:32,889 --> 00:08:36,589
(Now, it's time for me to sit on the throne.)

221
00:08:39,499 --> 00:08:42,799
(Picking up a thick strip of pork belly)

222
00:08:43,999 --> 00:08:46,499
(Cutting)

223
00:08:47,299 --> 00:08:48,539
This is for breakfast.

224
00:08:51,709 --> 00:08:53,839
(It should be filling like a royal meal.)

225
00:08:55,539 --> 00:08:56,979
(Sprinkling)

226
00:08:58,049 --> 00:09:00,349
(Seasoning it with salt)

227
00:09:02,319 --> 00:09:04,348
(Closing the lid)

228
00:09:04,349 --> 00:09:06,159
(Pressing the button)

229
00:09:07,119 --> 00:09:09,989
(She goes to the fridge after letting the meat get grilled.)

230
00:09:11,459 --> 00:09:14,159
(Grabbing containers)

231
00:09:17,469 --> 00:09:19,439
She's taking out some side dishes for the meat.

232
00:09:25,369 --> 00:09:26,739
Gosh, it smells great.

233
00:09:26,879 --> 00:09:30,649
(Transferring pickled victory onion)

234
00:09:35,419 --> 00:09:37,989
(This time, she opens up the kimchi container.)

235
00:09:38,449 --> 00:09:40,219
My gosh, it's nicely fermented.

236
00:09:40,959 --> 00:09:42,288
Gosh, I love kimchi.

237
00:09:42,289 --> 00:09:43,958
- It's so good. - Yes.

238
00:09:43,959 --> 00:09:45,359
(Transferring it onto the plate)

239
00:09:46,799 --> 00:09:48,319
I have five different types of kimchi.

240
00:09:48,699 --> 00:09:50,298
- This is crazy. - Cucumber kimchi.

241
00:09:50,299 --> 00:09:51,328
- Cucumber kimchi? - Yes.

242
00:09:51,329 --> 00:09:53,438
Next, young radish kimchi.

243
00:09:53,439 --> 00:09:56,008
- Seriously. That's my favorite. - Do you like it?

244
00:09:56,009 --> 00:09:58,249
- That's my favorite kimchi. - MINHO is getting excited.

245
00:09:58,769 --> 00:09:59,849
Young summer radish kimchi.

246
00:10:01,709 --> 00:10:03,778
They're the five different types of kimchi I have.

247
00:10:03,779 --> 00:10:05,379
(Plating five different types of kimchi)

248
00:10:06,219 --> 00:10:08,678
You have so many different types of kimchi like a kimchi expert.

249
00:10:08,679 --> 00:10:09,919
She's like a kimchi researcher.

250
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:14,059
(Kimchi is ready.)

251
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:18,089
(Is the meat cooked?)

252
00:10:18,889 --> 00:10:19,959
Good.

253
00:10:22,969 --> 00:10:24,628
Oh, this is crazy.

254
00:10:24,629 --> 00:10:25,699
What is it?

255
00:10:26,669 --> 00:10:28,415
- Is it grilled nicely? Gosh. - It's grilled perfectly.

256
00:10:28,439 --> 00:10:29,539
Isn't this amazing?

257
00:10:29,869 --> 00:10:32,038
It rotates on its own.

258
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:33,778
I can put the meat in, close the lid,

259
00:10:33,779 --> 00:10:34,938
and do something else.

260
00:10:34,939 --> 00:10:36,209
That's convenient.

261
00:10:36,609 --> 00:10:38,249
