00:21:17,449 --> 00:21:18,549
(Struggling)

524
00:21:19,549 --> 00:21:20,618
My gosh.

525
00:21:20,619 --> 00:21:24,089
(She fixes the angle and tries to push it.)

526
00:21:24,129 --> 00:21:25,189
Wait.

527
00:21:29,299 --> 00:21:30,428
(The more she pushes, the wider the dirt stains smudge.)

528
00:21:30,429 --> 00:21:32,275
- It's getting dirtier. - It's getting dirtier.

529
00:21:32,299 --> 00:21:33,619
You can't see out the window now.

530
00:21:33,669 --> 00:21:36,169
- It's gotten murkier. - A privacy protection window.

531
00:21:38,169 --> 00:21:40,579
(The more she wipes, the tighter security grows.)

532
00:21:41,279 --> 00:21:42,639
I might be doing a bad job.

533
00:21:45,909 --> 00:21:47,648
I should turn it.

534
00:21:47,649 --> 00:21:49,095
(There's no way my revolutionary item will disappoint me.)

535
00:21:49,119 --> 00:21:50,588
This must be it.

536
00:21:50,589 --> 00:21:52,019
(Sounding certain)

537
00:21:53,089 --> 00:21:54,889
(Pushing)

538
00:21:56,289 --> 00:21:57,289
This is it?

539
00:21:57,489 --> 00:21:58,729
You have such short arms.

540
00:22:00,459 --> 00:22:02,829
My window didn't open all the way.

541
00:22:02,899 --> 00:22:04,628
- I get it. I see your problem. - Right.

542
00:22:04,629 --> 00:22:05,798
That's not going to work.

543
00:22:05,799 --> 00:22:08,098
- If it stains... - It might be useful for Sung Hwan.

544
00:22:08,099 --> 00:22:10,179
- I... That's good. - The window slides all the way.

545
00:22:10,239 --> 00:22:12,119
It'd be easier if it were a full-length window.

546
00:22:13,609 --> 00:22:15,709
I just think you don't know how to work it yet.

547
00:22:17,079 --> 00:22:18,508
I should look up how to use it.

548
00:22:18,509 --> 00:22:21,749
(Taking a step back)

549
00:22:23,179 --> 00:22:25,688
I have this habit of not reading the manual.

550
00:22:25,689 --> 00:22:27,519
- Same here. I don't read them. - Right.

551
00:22:27,759 --> 00:22:30,129
This time around, I read it after scanning the QR code.

552
00:22:31,629 --> 00:22:32,759
(Tapping)

553
00:22:38,369 --> 00:22:41,468
(To make matters worse, the video is in Chinese.)

554
00:22:41,469 --> 00:22:44,029
It felt like I was watching "A Better Tomorrow" all of a sudden.

555
00:22:45,809 --> 00:22:47,438
(A Chinese listening exam begins without any warning.)

556
00:22:47,439 --> 00:22:48,738
You just need to check the posture...

557
00:22:48,739 --> 00:22:50,579
- without the explanation. - You don't need...

558
00:22:53,049 --> 00:22:56,548
(As she needs help, she starts watching.)

559
00:22:56,549 --> 00:22:57,589
I attached it too.

560
00:22:59,689 --> 00:23:02,659
(Super focused)

561
00:23:03,459 --> 00:23:05,428
(The explanation continues in Chinese she doesn't understand.)

562
00:23:05,429 --> 00:23:06,558
(Stopping)

563
00:23:06,559 --> 00:23:07,858
- What? - That's it?

564
00:23:07,859 --> 00:23:09,858
- You could assemble it. - He didn't show me how to use it.

565
00:23:09,859 --> 00:23:11,298
He only showed you how to assemble it.

566
00:23:11,299 --> 00:23:12,768
- Right. - Not how to use it on windows?

567
00:23:12,769 --> 00:23:14,538
- He didn't show me that. - He didn't do that in the video.

568
00:23:14,539 --> 00:23:16,498
Right. All I understood from the video was "hello."

569
00:23:16,499 --> 00:23:17,969
(Dumbfounded)

570
00:23:19,039 --> 00:23:21,009
I waited a month for this. This is bad.

571
00:23:21,309 --> 00:23:22,309
It's not easy.

572
00:23:22,879 --> 00:23:23,879
Let me try it.

573
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:26,009
(Let me try it.)

574
00:23:27,249 --> 00:23:29,018
"Clean your windows easily."

575
00:23:29,019 --> 00:23:31,419
(I must finish cleaning the windows on my precious day off.)

576
00:23:31,489 --> 00:23:33,588
(Pushing down)

577
00:23:33,589 --> 00:23:34,659
This...

578
00:23:35,589 --> 00:23:37,089
What is this? Darn it.

579
00:23:39,059 --> 00:23:40,658
It's gotten dirtier, Shin Young.

580
00:23:40,659 --> 00:23:42,498
(Dirty)

581
00:23:42,499 --> 00:23:45,369
What is this? It's nothing like what I saw in the video.

582
00:23:46,669 --> 00:23:48,868
Gosh, I'm never buying this again.

583
00:23:48,869 --> 00:23:50,738
See? It was different from the video.

584
00:23:50,739 --> 00:23:51,739
Why isn't it working?

585
00:23:51,839 --> 00:23:53,878
My gosh. What is this?

586
00:23:53,879 --> 00:23:54,879
(Shaking)

587
00:23:57,049 --> 00:23:58,548
Gosh, I think it could work.

588
00:23:58,549 --> 00:23:59,808
I think so too.

589
00:23:59,809 --> 00:24:01,178
You might have to move it...

590
00:24:01,179 --> 00:24:02,548
- like you're sawing. - Right.

591
00:24:02,549 --> 00:24:04,618
Or you should hold just the bottom part in your house.

592
00:24:04,619 --> 00:24:06,718
- Gosh, I'm never buying this again. - You do have a short reach.

593
00:24:06,719 --> 00:24:08,419
- Yes. I'm too short. - You know?

594
00:24:09,619 --> 00:24:11,028
I waited a month for this.

595
00:24:11,029 --> 00:24:12,728
(Feeling dejected)

596
00:24:12,729 --> 00:24:13,849
I'm never buying this again.

597
00:24:14,799 --> 00:24:16,458
According to the videos I saw,

598
00:24:16,459 --> 00:24:18,999
it should stick to the window and I should be able to wipe it.

599
00:24:19,229 --> 00:24:20,498
When I put it over the window...

600
00:24:20,499 --> 00:24:21,798
I don't know what happened. Maybe, the mop was upset.

601
00:24:21,799 --> 00:24:24,538
- The head of the mop was sulking. - It went like this.

602
00:24:24,539 --> 00:24:26,139
- I was so upset. - Seriously.

603
00:24:26,779 --> 00:24:30,109
Later, I tried to wipe the bottom window.

604
00:24:30,509 --> 00:24:32,849
I thought my rotator cuff was going to tear off.

605
00:24:33,479 --> 00:24:36,519
Criminals get arrested by the FBI with their hands behind their backs.

606
00:24:36,719 --> 00:24:40,019
It made me wonder if that was how the criminals felt.

607
00:24:40,359 --> 00:24:42,518
Everyone says not giving in is the way to go.

608
00:24:42,519 --> 00:24:43,728
But I gave in completely.

609
00:24:43,729 --> 00:24:44,888
(Zero motivation)

610
00:24:44,889 --> 00:24:46,365
- It was a mess. - Nothing went well that day.

611
00:24:46,389 --> 00:24:48,398
- There are days like that. - Of course.

612
00:24:48,399 --> 00:24:49,428
You must be upset.

613
00:24:49,429 --> 00:24:50,498
- You waited for a long time. - Right.

614
00:24:50,499 --> 00:24:52,428
- Wasting time is the annoying part. - I was upset for sure.

615
00:24:52,429 --> 00:24:55,199
But I discover useful items...

616
00:24:55,369 --> 00:24:57,108
after several failures.

617
00:24:57,109 --> 00:24:58,109
Of course.

618
00:24:59,469 --> 00:25:01,079
(Wringing)

619
00:25:03,709 --> 00:25:04,879
What's this?

620
00:25:06,009 --> 00:25:07,169
I can just wipe it like this.

621
00:25:07,219 --> 00:25:08,379
I used my bare hands instead.

622
00:25:08,619 --> 00:25:10,118
- Not the mop. - You can only wipe that part.

623
00:25:10,119 --> 00:25:12,649
(She ends up abandoning the mop and using her bare hands.)

624
00:25:14,389 --> 00:25:16,688
My gosh. I didn't know the stains smeared on my arm.

625
00:25:16,689 --> 00:25:17,929
(Her arm is messy with stains.)

626
00:25:19,289 --> 00:25:22,359
(I should at least wipe the windowsills thoroughly.)

627
00:25:22,859 --> 00:25:24,369
My gosh. Yes. It looks clean enough.

628
00:25:25,999 --> 00:25:27,069
All done.

629
00:25:29,069 --> 00:25:31,769
(The windowsill looked blackish.)

630
00:25:32,539 --> 00:25:33,878
- It's clean. - It's clean now.

631
00:25:33,879 --> 00:25:35,178
- Gosh, I love it. - It's not easy...

632
00:25:35,179 --> 00:25:36,438
to clean the windowsill spotless like that.

633
00:25:36,439 --> 00:25:37,479
(Impressed)

634
00:25:39,049 --> 00:25:42,979
(The window was stained with dust.)

635
00:25:44,089 --> 00:25:45,818
(It's gotten a unique look.)

636
00:25:45,819 --> 00:25:47,188
I have to hope it rains soon.

637
00:25:47,189 --> 00:25:48,565
- The rainy season will last long. - You ruined it.

638
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:51,628
Neat freaks like Shin Young would hate seeing that.

639
00:25:51,629 --> 00:25:53,388
- Gosh, I don't want... - Seeing stains on the window...

640
00:25:53,389 --> 00:25:55,029
- to look out the windows now. - Exactly.

641
00:25:56,499 --> 00:25:59,128
I couldn't understand the reviews since they were in Chinese.

642
00:25:59,129 --> 00:26:00,939
(Lamenting)

643
00:26:01,939 --> 00:26:03,539
Gosh, I learned a lesson.

644
00:26:04,039 --> 00:26:05,269
I learned a lesson.

645
00:26:05,639 --> 00:26:07,638
This was a good lesson I learned.

646
00:26:07,639 --> 00:26:10,649
- Did you throw it out? - No, I just put it away.

647
00:26:10,749 --> 00:26:12,449
I actually want it.

648
00:26:12,579 --> 00:26:14,178
I'll give it to Sung Hwan.

649
00:26:14,179 --> 00:26:16,178
- No way. - I actually bought two.

650
00:26:16,179 --> 00:26:17,718
- Thank you. - I bought two.

651
00:26:17,719 --> 00:26:19,159
(It might be useful for your house.)

652
00:26:19,989 --> 00:26:21,158
It's been an hour.

653
00:26:21,159 --> 00:26:23,440
(I tried to wipe the windows for an hour. How upsetting.)

654
00:26:23,789 --> 00:26:25,429
(Opening up)

655
00:26:27,099 --> 00:26:29,059
- She used it as an excuse to eat. - What's that?

656
00:26:30,829 --> 00:26:33,798
I was sweating and it wasn't working, so...

657
00:26:33,799 --> 00:26:35,338
- Did you want a cold drink? - Yes.

658
00:26:35,339 --> 00:26:37,138
- There was no air conditioner. - That's right.

659
00:26:37,139 --> 00:26:38,168
- That's right. - I forgot about that.

660
00:26:38,169 --> 00:26:40,208
- After the failed attempt... - When there is no air conditioner,

661
00:26:40,209 --> 00:26:42,289
- even standing still is exhausting. - That's right.

662
00:26:43,649 --> 00:26:44,649
(To a cup that's full of ice cubes)

663
00:26:44,650 --> 00:26:45,749
- Zero sugar. - Yes.

664
00:26:46,409 --> 00:26:47,549
It must be cold.

665
00:26:50,049 --> 00:26:52,619
(It goes straight to her throat.)

666
00:26:54,559 --> 00:26:55,659
(Exclaiming)

667
00:26:56,159 --> 00:26:57,188
- It's cold. - That's the taste.

668
00:26:57,189 --> 00:26:58,189
That's right.

669
00:26:58,190 --> 00:27:00,558
On some days, Coke tastes better than a meal.

670
00:27:00,559 --> 00:27:01,559
That's right.

671
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:03,005
(It washes down the frustration from cleaning the windows.)

672
00:27:03,029 --> 00:27:06,939
(A glass of cold soft drink)

673
00:27:14,939 --> 00:27:15,979
What now?

674
00:27:16,439 --> 00:27:19,649
(She takes something out once her stomach is settled.)

675
00:27:22,119 --> 00:27:25,519
(I need to move busily to finish the chores on my day off.)

676
00:27:26,489 --> 00:27:29,789
(Heave-ho)

677
00:27:30,759 --> 00:27:33,458
(She moves the piled-up shoeboxes to the living room.)

678
00:27:33,459 --> 00:27:34,599
Those must be shoes.

679
00:27:35,799 --> 00:27:37,398
Throwing away the shoebox seems like a waste.

680
00:27:37,399 --> 00:27:38,628
- It's a waste. - That's right. I don't know why.

681
00:27:38,629 --> 00:27:39,629
- Right? - That's right.

682
00:27:42,439 --> 00:27:45,569
(The boxes pile up in no time.)

683
00:27:46,709 --> 00:27:49,038
The shoeboxes were piling up...

684
00:27:49,039 --> 00:27:50,709
because I didn't know where to put them.

685
00:27:50,949 --> 00:27:55,279
These days, I really want to try...

686
00:27:55,679 --> 00:27:58,049
creative craft.

687
00:27:58,319 --> 00:28:01,519
Instead of buying a new item, I wanted to use what I had...

688
00:28:01,989 --> 00:28:03,959
to create something new.

689
00:28:04,289 --> 00:28:05,688
Using the items at home,

690
00:28:05,689 --> 00:28:06,858
(What can I make at home?)

691
00:28:06,859 --> 00:28:08,458
I wanted to make something.

692
00:28:08,459 --> 00:28:11,369
I wanted to recycle. So I decided to use...

693
00:28:11,469 --> 00:28:13,198
the shoeboxes I had collected...

694
00:28:13,199 --> 00:28:14,699
to make a dresser.

695
00:28:14,969 --> 00:28:16,399
It's fun to watch you craft.

696
00:28:16,939 --> 00:28:19,438
- See that table with stickers? - I think it looks really cool.

697
00:28:19,439 --> 00:28:20,608
I made it myself.

698
00:28:20,609 --> 00:28:21,879
- That's a bit... - Yes.

699
00:28:22,079 --> 00:28:23,439
It's a vintage table.

700
00:28:26,179 --> 00:28:27,848
Using shoeboxes, I'll make a dresser.

701
00:28:27,849 --> 00:28:29,978
You want them to slide out like drawers.

702
00:28:29,979 --> 00:28:31,019
That's right.

703
00:28:33,589 --> 00:28:34,718
Using shoeboxes?

704
00:28:34,719 --> 00:28:36,759
(Curious)

705
00:28:38,259 --> 00:28:41,859
(She cuts the top to make the compartment.)

706
00:28:44,269 --> 00:28:46,369
(Let's see.)

707
00:28:48,969 --> 00:28:50,068
It doesn't fit.

708
00:28:50,069 --> 00:28:52,369
(It doesn't fit.)

709
00:28:53,609 --> 00:28:54,709
(Flustered)

710
00:28:54,909 --> 00:28:57,108
- Are the shoeboxes the same size? - That's right.

711
00:28:57,109 --> 00:28:58,908
- Don't they need to be different? - That's right.

712
00:28:58,909 --> 00:29:00,449
(Smart CODE KUNST)

713
00:29:01,679 --> 00:29:03,479
(She tries it with a different box.)

714
00:29:05,349 --> 00:29:07,989
(Thankfully, the size is perfect this time.)

715
00:29:08,689 --> 00:29:10,789
(The compartment can be pushed in and out.)

716
00:29:11,929 --> 00:29:15,199
(Can I glue them together like this?)

717
00:29:16,029 --> 00:29:18,399
(Let's see.)

718
00:29:19,799 --> 00:29:22,339
(But the boxes have slightly different heights.)

719
00:29:23,099 --> 00:29:24,508
This isn't what I planned.

720
00:29:24,509 --> 00:29:27,078
(Flustered)

721
00:29:27,079 --> 00:29:28,079
Then...

722
00:29:30,239 --> 00:29:32,208
(The dresser faces a crisis.)

723
00:29:32,209 --> 00:29:33,448
(I can't...)

724
00:29:33,449 --> 00:29:35,649
- "I can't." - That's genius.

725
00:29:36,419 --> 00:29:38,218
(What should I do?)

726
00:29:38,219 --> 00:29:39,649
The boxes were supposed...

727
00:29:40,019 --> 00:29:42,759
to go into other boxes prettily.

728
00:29:42,959 --> 00:29:45,959
But they didn't go in since they were the same size.

729
00:29:46,159 --> 00:29:48,129
So I decided to make a table...

730
00:29:48,359 --> 00:29:50,829
where I could display a plastic model...

731
00:29:50,999 --> 00:29:53,069
and got to work.

732
00:29:53,199 --> 00:29:54,339
A table for a plastic model?

733
00:29:54,469 --> 00:29:56,298
When something doesn't work, I give up quickly.

734
00:29:56,299 --> 00:29:57,908
- That's a good habit. - I give up quickly.

735
00:29:57,909 --> 00:29:59,138
If I try to make it work,

736
00:29:59,139 --> 00:30:00,808
- my entire day will be wasted. - And you'll get stressed out.

737
00:30:00,809 --> 00:30:01,839
That's right.

738
00:30:02,839 --> 00:30:04,979
I'll go with the initial plan.

739
00:30:05,949 --> 00:30:07,819
(Loading up the glue gun)

740
00:30:08,849 --> 00:30:10,649
- You have that at home? - Yes.

741
00:30:13,049 --> 00:30:14,388
- She put the boxes together. - Yes.

742
00:30:14,389 --> 00:30:16,418
(She begins building without hesitation.)

743
00:30:16,419 --> 00:30:18,828
That goes on the bottom.

744
00:30:18,829 --> 00:30:20,698
(After giving up quickly, she works just as quickly.)

745
00:30:20,699 --> 00:30:21,799
You're like MacGyver.

746
00:30:23,659 --> 00:30:27,899
(She stacks up the boxes to make a display table.)

747
00:30:30,939 --> 00:30:35,739
(She puts on her glasses to focus on the craft.)

748
00:30:37,609 --> 00:30:41,819
(She creates the idea that enters her head.)

749
00:30:46,249 --> 00:30:47,259
(Sighing)

750
00:30:47,389 --> 00:30:50,489
(I think it's pretty much done.)

751
00:30:51,329 --> 00:30:55,059
(Let's put it on display.)

752
00:30:55,359 --> 00:30:56,399
That's right.

753
00:31:00,939 --> 00:31:02,899
- It works. - What? It looks pretty.

754
00:31:03,499 --> 00:31:04,508
(The light comes on.)

755
00:31:04,509 --> 00:31:05,509
It's like a display table.

756
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:06,769
- That's right. - I see.

757
00:31:08,509 --> 00:31:09,679
It looks legit.

758
00:31:10,609 --> 00:31:11,679
Let's turn off the lights.

759
00:31:13,179 --> 00:31:15,139
- You should turn off the lights. - That's right.

760
00:31:15,879 --> 00:31:18,089
(Shining bright)

761
00:31:18,919 --> 00:31:20,088
(It makes them exclaim.)

762
00:31:20,089 --> 00:31:21,218
- Doesn't it look nice? - It's pretty.

763
00:31:21,219 --> 00:31:23,158
- The LED light is pretty. - That's right.

764
00:31:23,159 --> 00:31:25,228
- It's a good idea. - You made an atmospheric piece...

765
00:31:25,229 --> 00:31:26,458
- using shoeboxes. - Doesn't it look nice?

766
00:31:26,459 --> 00:31:28,529
Such pieces of furniture can be expensive.

767
00:31:28,999 --> 00:31:30,399
It looks really cool.

768
00:31:31,899 --> 00:31:34,198
Not bad. It's pretty.

769
00:31:34,199 --> 00:31:36,839
(She failed to make a dresser but managed to make something else.)

770
00:31:37,539 --> 00:31:38,838
Shin Young, it's pretty.

771
00:31:38,839 --> 00:31:39,969
- I know. - It's hip.

772
00:31:40,139 --> 00:31:41,779
Gosh, it sets the mood.

773
00:31:44,349 --> 00:31:46,409
(I can't believe I made it myself.)

774
00:31:46,879 --> 00:31:48,749
- It's so pretty. - It's nice.

775
00:31:50,019 --> 00:31:52,089
- It's cool. - I love it so much.

776
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,259
I'm 100 percent satisfied with it.

777
00:31:54,459 --> 00:31:56,489
I thought of what to do next.

778
00:31:56,759 --> 00:31:58,759
You know the building blocks, right?

779
00:31:59,059 --> 00:32:00,858
I want to put them on top.

780
00:32:00,859 --> 00:32:03,059
(Satisfied, she came up with a plan for the next item.)

781
00:32:03,899 --> 00:32:06,305
